# The card only. The eMMC (mmc2) isn't even enabled in the device tree.
#
# By LABEL, not PARTUUID: the kernel resolves root=PARTUUID itself, but
# userspace here is busybox + mdev, which makes no /dev/disk/by-partuuid links.
# Third card test: fsck.fat was handed "PARTUUID=f4a3e001-01" as a path, failed,
# and OpenRC's fsck aborted the boot runlevel (rc-abort) -- so networking,
# dropbear, wpa_supplicant and frame-diag never ran on any of the first three
# boots. Not a device path either: the card came up as mmcblk1, so the numbering
# follows probe order and isn't ours to rely on. busybox mount resolves LABEL
# from /proc/partitions without any links.
#
# fsck pass 0 for both: root is ext4 with a journal, already mounted rw by the
# kernel; /boot is the FAT the Mac writes to, and a dirty bit there must never
# stop the frame from coming up. nofail on /boot for the same reason.
LABEL=frameroot	/	ext4	rw,noatime	0 0
LABEL=FRAMEBOOT	/boot	vfat	rw,noatime,nofail,fmask=0177,dmask=0077	0 0
tmpfs	/tmp	tmpfs	nosuid,nodev	0 0
